    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine is well-positioned for today\u2019s slate, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Kyle Tucker** (75.19). **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our premier play; his matchup against a mid-tier right-hander in a favorable park, combined with his dual-threat ability to steal bases, creates an elite projection despite the opposing pitcher's moderate hold rate. **Kyle Tucker** also remains a core start; despite a tough assignment against a left-hander, his raw base output remains high enough to transcend matchup volatility. Furthermore, **Jacob Wilson** (74.07) is a highlight play; he draws a favorable matchup against a starter with a high 5.23 xERA, providing a rare opportunity to exploit a soft pitching rotation at the top of our order.\n\nBeyond our top-tier starts, we are capitalizing on several situational edges. **Josh Lowe** (62.77) and **Jackson Merrill** (63.85) both benefit from favorable stolen base environments, as our models account for the slow delivery times of their respective opposing pitchers, adding valuable percentage points to their overall efficiency. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.69) also sees a significant boost from a high-leverage matchup against a starter with an xERA of 5.58, making him a primary source for RBI production today. The most difficult personnel decision was leaving **Brayan Rocchio** (59.25) on the bench. While his projection is strong, he ultimately fell short of the starting cut because **Sam Antonacci** (61.26) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.08) offer superior situational platoon advantages against their specific opponents. \n\nWhile the outlook is strong, we remain cautious regarding **Drake Baldwin** (53.95) and **Liam Hicks** (44.72). Both are starts, but they face pitchers with respectable xERAs, and **Liam Hicks** specifically faces a dynamic platoon disadvantage that suppresses his scoring ceiling. No acute weather threats are currently impacting the venue, but we will monitor the lineup status for **Drake Baldwin** and **Sam Antonacci** to ensure their spot at the top of the order remains locked, as their projection heavily relies on those plate appearances to maximize their stolen base and run-scoring potential.",
